    <GaugingStation location="County Bridge Euston" name="Little Ouse" number="33011">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound weir gauging a Chalk catchment with predominantly agricultural land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">One rating applied across period of record. Hydraulic model used to derive rating for peak flows, including out of bank and bypassing. Reasonable fit to gaugings. Part of the Thet-Little Ouse groundwater support scheme, which triggers at 95 l/s to maintain flow.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound weir with triangular profile centre section, 3.4m broad; broad-crested flanks in trapezoidal channel 9m broad.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Peak flows available from 1960. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Groundwater abstractions for PWS and spray irrigation. Some effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Chalk with significant Boulder Clay cover. Agricultural land use, predominantly arable.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 18% of AMAX3. Confident in hydraulic model derived rating and extrapolation." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
